; assistant: a resident agent you talk to by leaving it messages. Each
; message wakes a model for one turn of the same conversation, so it
; remembers all of it, days apart; its answer lands in your inbox. Replying
; to an answer is your next message, and messages that come while it answers
; wait their turn. It has no tools: it reads what you send and answers.
; It runs on huff, on Kimi K2 through OpenRouter: the daemon needs
; OPENROUTER_API_KEY. Its conversation is puff data in its home.
;   whiff call assistant/tell "the release is on Friday; remind me what's left"
;   whiff inbox                  ; its answer, from :assistant
;   whiff reply 7 "and the docs?"   ; the next message; or :seen to dismiss
;
;   whiff call assistant/ask "what's left?"  ; pending; whiff wait <id> has the answer
;   whiff call assistant/forget  ; start a new conversation
;
; Its home is ~/.whiff/agents/<its name>. For another agent, write another
; (agent name :prompt "...") file; :model picks the model, a provider's as
; here or a Claude model ("" for Claude's default, "opus"), which runs on
; the claude CLI; :can [:gh/prs :todo/add] gives it those whiff functions
; as tools (another agent's :helper/ask too, whose answer comes back as a
; turn), and :every 1d gives it a turn of its own each day, which answers
; only with news.

(agent assistant
  :prompt "Help the user keep track of what they tell you."
  :model "openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2")
